// Expected verdict from J. Pichon-Pharabod and P. Sewell, "A Concurrency Semantics for Relaxed Atomics that Permits Optimisation and Avoids Thin-Air Executions", POPL 2016, not a numbered example: forbidden by §6's no-thin-air argument for arithmetic-free programs; checked here under sMRD.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  r1 := x;
  y := r1
} ||| {
  r2 := y;
  x := r2
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 42 && r2 = 42) [sMRD]